## 2. COLOR SYSTEM

### Primary Palette (use these and only these)

```
--color-deep-teal:     #0D4A5C   /* Primary actions, headings, trust anchor */
--color-mid-teal:      #1A7A9A   /* Secondary actions, links, progress */
--color-light-teal:    #D6EEF5   /* Teal tints, info backgrounds */

--color-sage:          #6B9E7A   /* Success, completion, positive findings */
--color-sage-light:    #E8F3EB   /* Success backgrounds, section complete */

--color-coral:         #E8634A   /* Safety alerts, Pathway B, critical flags */
--color-coral-light:   #FDECEA   /* Alert backgrounds, symptom interrupt bg */

--color-amber:         #D4873A   /* Warnings, "needs attention", interaction flags */
--color-amber-light:   #FDF3E4   /* Warning backgrounds */

--color-cream:         #FAF8F5   /* App background — not pure white, never grey */
--color-white:         #FFFFFF   /* Card surfaces */
--color-charcoal:      #1C2329   /* Primary text */
--color-slate:         #4A5568   /* Secondary text */
--color-mist:          #9AA5B4   /* Placeholder text, disabled */
--color-border:        #E2E8F0   /* Subtle borders, dividers */
--color-shadow:        rgba(13,74,92,0.08) /* Shadows use teal-tinted black */
```

**Why this palette:**
- Deep teal (not blue) signals clinical precision without the sterile coldness
  of hospital blue. It's also rare enough to be distinctive.
- Sage green for positive findings and completion — psychologically associated
  with safety, growth, and nature. Avoids "you passed" harshness.
- Coral (not red) for alerts — serious but not alarming. Red causes fight-or-
  flight; coral says "pay attention" without panic.
- Cream background (not white, not grey) — white is clinical/cold, grey is
  depressing. Cream is warm, readable, and premium.

**What NOT to do:**
- No generic health-app blue (#2196F3, #1976D2 etc.) — those read as insurance
  apps and hospital portals.
- No bright green (too cheerful for a serious topic).
- No red for anything except a true emergency exit (Pathway B button only).
- No dark mode in Phase 1-2 — the pale cream palette is core to the emotional
  tone. Dark mode is a Phase 5+ consideration.

### Semantic Color Rules
```
Action primary:    --color-deep-teal     (all primary CTAs)
Action secondary:  --color-mid-teal      (secondary buttons, links)
Success:           --color-sage          (section complete, normal result)
Warning:           --color-amber         (needs attention, interaction flag)
Danger:            --color-coral         (symptom alert, Pathway B, critical)
Information:       --color-light-teal bg (educational tooltips, info cards)
Disabled:          --color-border bg + --color-mist text
```

