## 5. COMPONENT LIBRARY (build each one, reuse everywhere)

Cursor: build every component below before building any screen. Screens are
assembled from these components. If a screen needs something not in this list,
add it to this list first, then use it.

### 5.1 Button System

**PrimaryButton** — the one action on a screen the user should take next
```
Background:  --color-deep-teal
Text:        white, Inter 15sp 600
Height:      56px (taller than standard — easier tap target for anxious hands)
Width:       full-width minus horizontal padding
Radius:      12px
Shadow:      button-shadow
Pressed:     scale(0.97) + 10% darker background
Disabled:    --color-border bg, --color-mist text, no shadow
Loading:     replace label with a teal spinner, keep dimensions
```

**SecondaryButton** — an alternative, less important action
```
Background:  transparent
Border:      1.5px --color-deep-teal
Text:        --color-deep-teal, Inter 15sp 600
Height:      52px
Radius:      12px
Pressed:     --color-light-teal background
```

**TextButton** — low-emphasis action (skip, cancel, "learn more")
```
Background:  none
Text:        --color-mid-teal, Inter 15sp 400, underline on press only
Height:      44px (minimum tap target)
```

**DangerButton** — Pathway B exit ONLY (the one time we use coral as primary)
```
Background:  --color-coral
Text:        white, Inter 15sp 600
Height:      56px
Radius:      12px
Use ONLY for: "See a doctor now" / Pathway B CTA
```

**IconButton** — square tap target for navigation icons
```
Size:        44×44px (accessibility minimum)
Radius:      10px
Pressed:     --color-light-teal background
```

### 5.2 Input Fields

All inputs follow this same anatomy:
```
Container:   white bg, 1.5px --color-border border, 10px radius, 56px height
Focus:       1.5px --color-mid-teal border + subtle teal glow (shadow 0 0 0 3px rgba(26,122,154,0.12))
Error:       1.5px --color-coral border
Label:       12sp Inter 500 --color-slate, above the field (not placeholder-only)
Placeholder: --color-mist
Value:       15sp Inter 400 --color-charcoal
```

Component variants:
- **TextInput** — standard single-line
- **NumberInput** — numeric keyboard, with +/- stepper buttons for small values
- **DatePicker** — bottom sheet calendar, not a text field
- **SelectPicker** — bottom sheet list, not a native dropdown
- **RadioGroup** — large tap-target radio buttons (full-width cards, not small dots)
- **CheckboxGroup** — same large-card style, multi-select
- **Slider** — for stress level 1-10 if needed later

**RadioGroup card style (critical for questionnaire UX):**
```
Each option = a full-width card
Unselected: white bg, --color-border border, 14px radius
Selected:   --color-light-teal bg, 2px --color-mid-teal border, checkmark icon right
Height:     56px minimum
Text:       15sp Inter 500 --color-charcoal
Spacing:    8px between options
```
Why full-width cards instead of dots: research shows people complete more of a
form when options feel substantial. Tiny radio dots feel test-like and clinical.
Big cards feel like a considered choice.

### 5.3 ClinicalTerm Component (from Phase 2 — must match this spec exactly)
```
Container:  white card, card-shadow, 16px padding, 14px radius
Row 1:      plainName — 17sp Inter 600 --color-charcoal
Row 2:      plainExplanation — 14sp Inter 400 --color-slate, 4px below row 1
Divider:    1px --color-border, 12px vertical margin
Row 3:      "Clinical name:" label 11sp Inter 500 --color-mist
            medicalName 13sp DM Mono 400 --color-slate
Info icon:  right of row 1, tapping opens a bottom-sheet with more detail
```

### 5.4 Progress Components

**QuestionnaireStepper** — the top bar on every questionnaire screen
```
Background: white
Content:    "Section 3 of 10" in 13sp Inter 500 --color-slate
            Thin progress bar below: --color-sage fill, --color-border track
            4px height, full width, smooth animated fill
```
Why show section number AND a bar: the number answers "where am I", the bar
answers "how much remains". Both together reduce anxiety about the unknown length.

**JourneyProgressCard** — the home screen tracker
```
Steps displayed as a vertical timeline, not a horizontal stepper (easier to read
on mobile, scales to 6+ steps without crowding)
Completed step: --color-sage dot, sage text
Current step:   --color-deep-teal dot (pulsing animation), bold text, "Continue" chip
Upcoming step:  --color-border dot, --color-mist text
```

**SectionCompleteCard** — shown immediately when a questionnaire section saves
```
Background: --color-sage-light
Icon:       checkmark in a sage circle (not a toast — a full inline moment)
Title:      "Section complete" — DM Serif Display 20sp --color-sage
Subtitle:   plain encouragement, e.g. "You're 3 of 10 done. Keep going."
Duration:   shown for 1.5 seconds, then auto-advances. Never blocks indefinitely.
```
Psychology: this micro-celebration triggers a small dopamine hit that keeps
people going through a long questionnaire. It costs nothing and dramatically
reduces drop-off.

### 5.5 Alert & Safety Components

**SymptomInterruptCard** — the mid-questionnaire safety gate
```
Background:  --color-coral-light
Border:      2px --color-coral, left border only (like a sidebar callout)
Icon:        ⚠ in coral (not 🚨 — urgent but not panicked)
Title:       "One important question" — 17sp Inter 600 --color-coral
Body:        the question text — 15sp Inter 400 --color-charcoal
Buttons:     full-width RadioGroup cards: "No, I haven't" (teal) / "Yes, I have" (coral)
```
The left-border-only style (like an editorial callout) signals importance
without filling the screen with red and triggering panic.

**PathwayBBanner** — after routing to Pathway B
```
Background:  --color-cream (calm, not a red screen of doom)
Icon:        a phone/doctor icon in teal (action-oriented, not alarming)
Title:       "Let's get you the right care" — DM Serif 24sp --color-deep-teal
Body:        warm, directive — "Based on your answers, seeing a doctor soon is the
             right next step. This app will be here when you're ready to return."
CTA:         DangerButton "Find a doctor" (actually coral here, not deep-teal)
Secondary:   TextButton "Save my place"
```
Psychology: the worst thing this screen can do is look like an error or a
rejection. The user has done nothing wrong. The copy and design must feel like
a caring hand-off, not a dismissal.

**IodineHardStop** — the iodine contraindication block
```
Background:  --color-amber-light
Border:      1px --color-amber
Icon:        ⚠ in amber
Title:       "This isn't recommended for you right now"
Body:        plain reason — "Because your thyroid antibodies are positive,
             iodine supplementation could cause a flare-up. Your plan has been
             adjusted to keep you safe."
```

**InteractionFlag** — supplement that needs practitioner check
```
Badge on card:  amber pill chip "Needs practitioner check"
On detail:      amber callout box with the plain reason
```

### 5.6 Cards

**ResultCard**
```
White bg, card-shadow, 16px padding, 14px radius
Left edge: 4px vertical colour bar (sage=normal, amber=attention, coral=critical)
Row 1: plainName 16sp Inter 600 --color-charcoal
Row 2: status chip (see 5.7) + plain one-line meaning
Row 3: "Medical name:" + DM Mono 13sp (secondary, smaller)
Tap: opens Result Detail screen
```

**InterventionCard**
```
White bg, card-shadow, 16px padding, 14px radius
Top-left: category icon (see Section 6)
Title: 16sp Inter 600
Why: "Why you're seeing this:" label + one-line plain reason
Expand: "Clinical basis ›" collapsed by default — expands to show exact
        protocol wording
Status badge: sage "Approved" / amber "Pending review" / coral "Needs check"
```

**ProductCard** (store)
```
White bg, card-shadow
Image: 80×80px supplement/test illustration, left
Right: name 16sp, price 15sp Inter 600 --color-deep-teal
       one-line description 13sp --color-slate
       "Add" button: 32px height, teal, pill-shaped, right-aligned
Safety state: if blocked/flagged, badge replaces "Add" button
```

### 5.7 Status Chips / Badges
```
Normal/Complete:  sage bg + sage text: "Within range" / "Done"
Attention:        amber bg + amber text: "Worth watching" / "Pending"
Critical:         coral bg + coral text: "Needs attention" / "See doctor"
Approved:         deep-teal bg + white text: "Approved"
Draft:            border-only, slate text: "Pending review"
```
All chips: 12sp Inter 500, 6px horizontal padding, 4px vertical, 20px radius.
Never show raw lab values as the headline — chip first, value on detail.

