## 8. MOTION & ANIMATION

Less is more. One deliberate moment beats ten scattered effects.

**Principles:**
- Motion answers an action — screen transitions, expanding an accordion,
  completing a section. Never idle/looping animations.
- Duration: 200ms for micro (button press), 280ms for screen transitions,
  1.5s for the SectionCompleteCard hold. Nothing over 300ms for transitions.
- Easing: always ease-out (fast start, gentle end). Never linear.
- Respect `useReducedMotion` — detect it and cut all motion for users who have
  enabled it in accessibility settings.

**Specific animations to build:**
```
Button press:        scale(0.97) in 80ms, ease-out back in 120ms
Screen push:         translate X 30px → 0, opacity 0 → 1, 280ms ease-out
Screen pop:          reverse
QuestionnaireStepper fill: animated width change on section complete, 400ms ease-out
SectionCompleteCard: fade + scale in (0.95 → 1) 200ms, hold 1.5s, fade out 200ms
RadioGroup select:   border + bg colour change, 120ms
Status chip:         colour fade in 150ms when result loads
```

**What NOT to animate:**
- ❌ Page-load staggered list reveals (AI-generated default, avoid)
- ❌ Parallax or floating elements
- ❌ Lottie animations (adds app weight for minimal gain)
- ❌ Skeleton loaders that pulse in a disturbing heartbeat (use a static
  muted version instead)

