## 9. LOADING, EMPTY & ERROR STATES

Every state must be designed. No naked spinners. No blank white screens.

**Loading:**
- Show a static skeleton (ghost layout in --color-border, no pulse) for the
  initial data load on Results and Plan screens
- Inline spinner (teal, 20px) for button actions and saves
- Full-screen loading only for auth — all other loads happen behind already-
  rendered chrome

**Empty states:**
- Never just "No data found"
- Always: icon (Feather) + heading + one-line explanation + action if applicable
- Examples:
  - No results yet: "Your results will appear here once your tests are back."
  - Empty cart: "Nothing in your basket yet. Start from your personalised plan."
  - No follow-ups: "You're all caught up. Check back after your next test."

**Error states:**
- Toast for non-blocking errors (network timeout, save retry): bottom of screen,
  --color-amber-light bg, 3 second auto-dismiss, "Try again" link
- Inline for form errors: below the specific field, --color-coral, 13sp
- Full-screen for fatal errors (auth failure, app boot failure): icon +
  plain explanation + one action ("Try again" or "Log in again")
- Never: raw error codes, stack traces, or "Something went wrong" with no
  guidance

