## 11. NAVIGATION & INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE

**Bottom tab bar (5 tabs, always visible after onboarding):**
```
Home | Questionnaire | Results | Plan | More
```
- Active tab: deep teal icon + 13sp label
- Inactive: slate icon + slate label
- Never show the tab bar during the triage screen, Pathway B screen, or
  individual questionnaire section screens (focused task = no distractions)
- Tab bar has a subtle top border, white background, safe-area aware

**Back navigation:**
- Every screen inside a stack has a back arrow (Feather 'arrow-left', 24px, teal)
- Exception: Pathway B cannot be backed out of (the hardware back is intercepted
  and shows a bottom-sheet: "Are you sure? If you have symptoms, please see a
  doctor.")
- Questionnaire section "back" returns to the questionnaire hub (not the previous
  section) — because partially answered sections save automatically, there's no
  "back = undo" expectation to manage

**Questionnaire flow (the most complex navigation in the app):**
```
Hub (section list) → Section screen → SymptomInterrupt (if triggered) → next section
                  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────→ Hub (if back)
```

