## 12. COPYWRITING RULES (voice & tone)

Match the design: confident, warm, precise. Not chatty. Not clinical.

- **Sentence case everywhere** (not Title Case, never ALL CAPS for body)
- **Active voice:** "We check your stress hormone" not "Stress hormones are checked"
- **Specific over vague:** "This takes about 8 minutes" not "This takes a few minutes"
- **Never use:** "Please", "Sorry", "Unfortunately", "As an AI", "Note that"
- **For findings/results:** lead with what it means for you, not the raw number
- **For errors:** say what happened and what to do. "Your session expired. Log in again."
- **For safety alerts:** calm and directive. Never alarming. "Let's get you the right care."
- **Button labels:** verb + object. "Save answers" not "Submit". "See my plan" not "Next".
- **Section completion:** acknowledge effort. "Section 3 done — you're making real progress."
- **Empty states:** future-positive. "Your results will appear here" not "No results yet"

